      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-85965",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose that we wish to study the population of residents of a city. Which of the following samples would be representative of the population?\n\n1. A selection of $5$ of the mayor's family members.\n2. A selection of $10$ people whose addresses were randomly chosen from a list of all addresses in the city.\n3. A selection of $17$ people walking on a particular street at noon."
